{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"monarchal-flannel-towhee","creation_channel":"cli","description":"Move the GET-rotation stamp out of `bindings.json` so the file stops changing on passes with no\nreal change. After A1 this is what collapses the **version count** (20 of 40 sampled revisions\nbecome byte-identical), taking the combined saving to **12.8x**. session_log **1cb6-d553-6565-49b4** (measured facts; do not re-derive).\n\n## Why\n`set_last_get` (`binding_store.py:459-464`) stamps `last_get_pass` on up to `deletion_probe_limit`\n(default 20) bound-but-absent keys per pass. Measured: exactly **20 entries change per pass**. So\nwith A1 alone the file still changes every pass and the version count stays ~180/day; only the delta\nshrinks. Losing rotation state is harmless — it just resets ordering, and the existing wrappers at\n`outbound_differ.py:167-172` are already fail-open.\n\n## Approach — compatibility first\nWrite the new file, read `max(new, legacy)`, and **keep writing the legacy field**. Deletion is a\nseparate ticket (A2-2).\n\n`max()`, not new-then-old: under mixed versions an old binary advances the in-line field but cannot\nwrite the new file, so a first-wins read would take the **stale** value; since rotation sorts on it\n(`outbound_differ.py:607`), recently-probed keys would sort first and the rest would starve. Values\nare fixed-width zero-padded (`2026-07-29T21-46-44`), so lexicographic `max()` is chronological, and\n`_last_get_pass` returns `\"\"` on absence — the lexicographic minimum — so after A2-2 `max(new, \"\")`\ndegenerates cleanly to `new`.\n\n**Migrate in memory on load; persist only inside `save()` / the `if persist:` block**\n(`reconcile.py:547-549`). Adding a file IS a write, and `__main__.py:106` `_run_reconcile_check`\n(\"read-only\") reaches `load_binding_store` at `:152`. Not an ensure unit: `run_ensures` holds the\nstore filesystem lock (`ensures.py:155`), disjoint from `refs/reconciler/lock`, and\n`BindingStore.save()` takes no lock and is a whole-file `os.replace` — an ensure unit would introduce\na clobber race that does not exist today.\n\n**Module-size constraint:** `outbound_differ.py` is at **exactly 800 LOC**, the locked cap. This\nchange must be **net-negative** there — move `_last_get_pass` (`:155-163`) and `_set_last_get`\n(`:166-172`) into the new rotation module; the two call sites (`:607`, `:704`) are one-for-one\nsubstitutions.\n\n**Staging:** add `get_rotation.json` to `reconcile_helpers.py:206`'s `_rel_files` AND the basename\ncheck at `:227-230`, or it is never committed **locally** (GHA's `git add -A` would mask the\nomission). `.gitattributes` is a glob (`.bridge_state/* merge=ours`) so the new file is covered.\nUpdate `push.py:76`'s docstring, which names the regenerable files explicitly.\n\n## Rollback\nReverting is safe: readers fall back to the in-line field, which this change never stops writing, so\nrotation order survives and the orphaned file is inert.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The byte-identical/no-commit assertion from A1 **still holds when <=20 absent-key GETs occur in\n      a pass**. Tier: **integration** in a real temporary git repo.\n- [ ] `get_rotation.json` is **staged and committed locally** (asserted in a real temporary git repo,\n      since GHA's `git add -A` would mask a staging omission). Tier: **integration**.\n- [ ] Rotation order after an **interleaved old-binary/new-binary pass sequence** matches the\n      all-new sequence. Tier: **integration**. This is the RED case for the `max()` rule — a\n      first-wins read fails it.\n- [ ] A legacy store with in-line stamps only yields identical rotation order. Tier: **unit**.\n- [ ] `rebar reconcile-check` against a pre-migration store leaves the worktree byte-identical\n      (`git status --porcelain` empty). Tier: **CLI subprocess** + worktree assertion.\n- [ ] `wc -l src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/outbound_differ.py` is **<=800**. Verify: the\n      module-size gate in `_build-and-test.yml` passes.\n\n## Files\n`binding_store.py`, new rotation module under `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/`,\n`outbound_differ.py`, `reconcile_helpers.py`, `_store/push.py` (docstring), tests\n\nScope: M. Depends on A1.","id":"9594-1f1c-bcd1-4774","parent_id":"0303-692c-55dc-4a18","priority":1,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"story","title":"A2-1: move last_get_pass rotation bookkeeping into .bridge_state/get_rotation.json (write-new, read max(new, legacy))"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785372488628349001,"uuid":"0310427b-6072-4bb4-ad8e-3033ed4aaa2f"}